  "bars"
 ],
 "teaches": [
  "A computed explainer is a StepExplainer with count and captionIndex: the frame, the input slot and the end logic cost one call, and the algorithm sits in resources.variables over the bound step",
  "Bubble sort as a gated sorting network: each comparison is two expressions that apply only once @at has reached them, and the last ones are the list at this step. No hand-computed trace, so any six numbers work",
  "The number of passes in closed form: the largest count of bigger numbers before any number, plus one",
  "CellRow shows values, a compared pair and the settled part from expressions"
 ],
